---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Callout from "../components/Callout.astro";
import { SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";

export const prerender = true;
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Cookie policy | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
  description="Which cookies this radiology and medicolegal law resource uses: strictly necessary storage, the single optional Google Analytics cookie, and how to accept, reject or change your choice."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Cookies"
    title="Cookie policy"
    description="One optional analytics cookie — set only if you accept it — and the strictly necessary storage that keeps the site working. Nothing else."
  />

  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Cookies"
    paragraphs={[
      "UK law requires consent before storing anything on your device that is not strictly necessary. This site therefore asks first: the banner offers Accept analytics or Reject analytics, and nothing optional is set until you choose.",
      "Your choice is remembered on your own device. You can change it at any time through the Cookie settings link in the footer, which re-opens the banner.",
    ]}
    contents={[
      { href: "#necessary", label: "Strictly necessary" },
      { href: "#analytics", label: "Optional analytics" },
      { href: "#choice", label: "Your choice" },
      { href: "#managing", label: "Managing cookies" },
    ]}
    reviewed="September 2026"
  />

  <section class="band">
    <div class="container-page">
      <div class="doc space-y-14">
        <Section id="necessary" index="01" eyebrow="Always on" title="Strictly necessary storage" lead="What the site needs to function. No consent is required, and it cannot be switched off.">
          <table class="table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Name</th>
                <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
                <th scope="col">Expiry</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td class="text-slate-800"><code>ml-consent-v1</code> (localStorage)</td>
                <td>Remembers your cookie choice so the banner does not ask again. Not a cookie; nothing leaves your device.</td>
                <td>Until cleared</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="text-slate-800">Clerk session</td>
                <td>Keeps you signed in to the secure login area only. Casual readers never receive it.</td>
                <td>Session</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="text-slate-800">Cloudflare security</td>
                <td>Bot protection and load management set by the hosting platform.</td>
                <td>Short-lived</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </Section>
        <Section id="analytics" index="02" eyebrow="Optional" title="Analytics — only with consent" lead="A single Google Analytics 4 cookie, set only after you click Accept analytics.">
          <table class="table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col">Name</th>
                <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
                <th scope="col">Expiry</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td class="text-slate-800"><code>_ga*</code></td>
                <td>Google Analytics 4: aggregate page-read counts. IP anonymised; 14-month retention.</td>
                <td>Up to 2 years</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <Callout tone="key" title="Before you choose">
            <p>Until you accept, Google's tag loads in consent-denied mode: it cannot set cookies or send identifiers. Rejecting or ignoring the banner leaves it that way — the site works identically either way.</p>
          </Callout>
        </Section>
        <Section id="choice" index="03" eyebrow="Consent" title="How your choice works" lead="Withdrawing consent is as easy as giving it.">
          <ul class="list">
            <li><strong>Accept analytics</strong> — the _ga cookie may be set and page reads counted.</li>
            <li><strong>Reject analytics</strong> — nothing optional is set, and nothing is recorded.</li>
            <li><strong>Change your mind</strong> — the Cookie settings link in the footer re-opens the banner on any page.</li>
          </ul>
        </Section>
        <Section id="managing" index="04" eyebrow="Your browser" title="Managing cookies yourself" lead="Every browser also lets you control cookies directly.">
          <p class="para-sm border-t border-slate-200 pt-4">You can block or delete cookies in browser settings at any time; the ICO guidance at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/for-the-public/online/cookies" class="link">ico.org.uk</a> explains how. Blocking strictly necessary storage may stop sign-in working, but reading the reference material is unaffected. Questions: see the <a href="/privacy-notice" class="link">privacy notice</a>.</p>
        </Section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
